{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only two completed experiments: RNA-only (pca_n2000, singleprofile, acc=0.485) and multimodal (pca_n2000, resnet50, concat, singleprofile, acc=0.527). The ~4-point gain from adding image suggests a positive contribution, but we cannot yet tell whether image alone is a strong signal, whether RNA is the dominant modality, or whether the fusion is genuinely synergistic. Testing config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) completes the basic modality factorial and isolates the image contribution. This is the highest-information next step: if image alone is weak (~0.30), the multimodal gain is a small RNA-anchored boost and we should prioritize RNA encoders and fusion; if image alone is strong (~0.50+), the multimodal model may be underleveraging image and we should explore better image encoders or fusion strategies. Under a tight budget, resolving which modality drives performance is more foundational than tuning fusion or profile settings on top of an uncharacterized system."
}

